<title>FRANCE: Renault V.I. launches tour bus.</title>
<headline>Renault V.I. launches tour bus.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Renault V.I., the trucks division of Renault SA, launched the Iliad line of tour buses on Monday at an industry show in Paris.</p>
<p>The buses, built at the Annonay plant in the Ardeche, would come in nine models with lengths varying from 10.6 to 12 metres, two heights, 3.30 and 3.55 metres, and options for three motors ranging from 302 to 380 horsepower.</p>
<p>Renault V.I. said it aimed for 45 percent of the French tour bus market of 800 units next year and four percent of the European market of 3,800 buses.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
